EXT. FLOODED RICE TERRACE - FORWARD OBSERVATION POST - DAWN

Mist on green water. A sandbagged dugout at the edge of a terrace wall. SERGEANT AUGUSTIN MBEKI (30s, helmet, binoculars) lies on his belly scanning the far ridge. Beside him, CORPORAL TEODOR BRANDVOLD (20s, radio on his back) chews a stalk of grass.

                    MBEKI
          (to the dugout, loud)
          Nobody light a cigarette. I mean it.

Nobody answers. The dugout holds only the two of them. Mbeki lowers the binoculars.

                    BRANDVOLD
          Sarge, he's out there again.

                    MBEKI
          Who?

                    BRANDVOLD
          The farmer. The one with the buffalo.

Mbeki raises the binoculars. A man on the far terrace guides a water buffalo through the paddy, unhurried.

                    MBEKI
          He's been told to clear out.

                    BRANDVOLD
          He doesn't have anywhere to go, Sarge.

Mbeki lowers the glasses. He watches Brandvold for a long moment. Brandvold keeps his eyes on the water.

                    MBEKI
          (muttering)
          Neither do we.

                    BRANDVOLD
          What?

                    MBEKI
          Nothing. Get the radio. Tell HQ the farmer's working his field.

Brandvold unslings the radio. He holds the handset a while before pressing the key. Mbeki takes off his helmet, lays it on the sandbags, and watches the buffalo's slow progress across the shining paddy.

                    BRANDVOLD
          (into radio)
          Echo Three, this is Echo Three-One. All quiet at the post.

He lets go of the key. Mbeki rests his chin on his folded arms.

                    MBEKI
          (softly)
          All quiet.
